:"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9d9ffdde0bb758c8a2dddc264c33b72111a8975a.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 19 at 4:20PM MDT until August 19 at 6:30PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 420 PM MDT, emergency management reported thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain over the Middle Aspen Acres Burn Scar. Flash flooding is\nongoing.\n\nExcessive rainfall over the burn scar has resulted in debris flows.\nThe debris flow can consist of rock, mud, vegetation and other loose\nmaterials.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding in and around the Middle Aspen Acres Burn\nScar.\n\nSOURCE...Emergency management reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nMiddle Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nSan Isabel, Highway 165, Highway 78, stream crossings, and county\nroads within and immediately downstream of the burn scar.\n\nThis includes the following high risk locations...\nBeulah Water Intake, Northcreek Road county line to Red Mountain Camp\nand Northcreek Road from Red Mountain Camp to Beulah.\n\nEmergency Managers noted flooding in the Aspen Acres Campground and\nflooding on Highway 165  with debris flows.","ends":"2026-08-19T18:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Custer, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.60342c10a027da7cf41aa988cc3cfdfd4daf5237.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.60342c10a027da7cf41aa988cc3cfdfd4daf5237.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 19 at 1:40PM MDT until August 19 at 8:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\ncontinue to be possible over the Aspen Acres burn scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 8 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres burn scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres burn scar should prepare for potential debris flow. Be sure\nto stay up to date with information from local authorities. Heavy\nrainfall could trigger flash flooding of low-lying areas, street\nflooding, and debris flows in and near recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the burn scar, which may lead to flash flooding and\ndebris flows.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-19T20:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.89cf3d25e80748ae24a920d75305dbaccd47d33a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.89cf3d25e80748ae24a920d75305dbaccd47d33a.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-19T18:47:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 191847 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1247 PM MDT Wed Aug 19 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Burn scar flash flooding and marginally severe storms possible this evening. - Daily afternoon showers and storms will continue into early next week, along with slowly warming temperatures. && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH THURSDAY/... Issued at 1246 PM MDT Wed Aug 19 202","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-19T17:27:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 191727 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1127 AM MDT Wed Aug 19 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-201730- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","u